MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1821382666}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "If you get familiar with the available gestures it can make playing Word
    Dawg easier and more fun. All the actions that can be made from the buttons can
    be made using gestures. There are additional swiping gestures that are not available
    in the buttons. You can turn the buttons off from Custom Game Settings if you
    prefer.\r\n\r\nTo begin, tap one of the letters in the rack to start a new word.\r\n\nSwipte
    right on a new or modified word to submit it, same as hitting the Submit button.
    It will appear in the list of Display Words.\n\nTap one of the DIsplay Words.
    It will be displayed under the rack. We call this the Selected word.\n\nIf you
    make a mistake and want to deselect a letter, tap the letter either in the New
    word. You can aslo tap the letter in  the selected word or the rack, whchever
    one it originated. You can also swipe left to clear out all the letters. You
    can also hit the Cancel button to unselect everything.\n\nSwipe left on the rack
    to get new rack letters, same as hitting the Replace Rack button.\r\n\r\nSwipe
    left on your new/modified word to clear all the letters, same as the Clear button.\n\nSwipe
    left again on your empty new/modified word to reset and clear the selected word,
    same as the Reset button. Or you can click on a word from your list of words
    to select a different word to modify.\n\nSwipe right on the selected word to
    select all the unselected letters. This can be helpful if you are just adding
    letters to the end of a word. It can also be helpful to select all the remaining
    letters after some are selected.\n\r\n\rSwipe left on the selected word to clear
    and unselect any selected letters.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
